2026-10-20 21:18:23	net32o	iter=10	41a8aac9-70ee-4729-8afc-90c42d93420b	CATEGORY: equivariant architectures |  | Add polarity-aware clause-to-clause attention on top of the existing bipartite message passing. Each round would also pass a message between clauses that share variables. |  | 1. Build a signed clause-overlap matrix for each formula: S = ip·ipᵀ + inn·innᵀ − ip·innᵀ − inn·ipᵀ. Entries are positive when two clauses share literals with the same sign and negative when they conflict. Divide each row by its degree plus one. | 2. In each round, after computing the clause state hq, add a residual update: hq ← tanh(hq + (S·hq)·Wsk + (|S|·hq)·Wak). Initialise Wsk and Wak at 0.3 scale, so the network starts from the parent's behaviour. | 3. Purpose: the per-clause weights w_jl are supposed to make up for 3-cavity and non-neighbour interactions that the projection drops. Those interactions come from clauses that overlap, and the current variable↔clause messages only reach them indirectly. Direct, sign-aware clause-to-clause messages expose frustration (conflicting clause pairs) to the weight head. | 4. Transfer to n=20: S is invariant to permuting variables and clauses, and the row normalisation keeps its scale stable as m grows. The extra cost is one (m×m) einsum per round, which is small at m≈200.
